Okular bundles the unmodified MDX dictionary from skywind3000/ECDICT 1.0.28:
https://github.com/skywind3000/ECDICT/releases/tag/1.0.28

Archive: ecdict-mdx-28.zip (97,755,340 bytes)
SHA-256: b06a72a0cfc37485a0466ee62fb43137559ea75eea147d8b7715142faca2229f
MDX: 97,786,525 bytes
SHA-256: 275e71b58fd359bfe649af1cbee533ea81770bdbc53ec4a34567f84720a5751b

The upstream describes this as the Concise English-Chinese Dictionary Enhanced
Edition, with approximately 3.4 million entries. The release-tagged MIT license,
Copyright (c) 2017 Linwei, is included here and embedded alongside the dictionary.

CMake downloads and verifies the release archive when dictionary bundling is
enabled. The large binary is kept in the build directory rather than Git.
No download occurs at runtime. Only the MDX is needed for the plain-text lookup
summary; no MDD, CSS, audio, or other external resources are required.
